  "priorExpiration": "2013-12-03",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Elec 303.06 Approval of High/Medium Voltage Trainee.\n\n(a) A high/medium voltage trainee identification card shall be issued when the applicant:\n\n(1) Submits a completed application pursuant to Elec 302.02(h), along with the fee required by (d) below;\n\n(2) Meets the qualification requirements of Elec 304.04;\n\n(3) Has no disqualifying felony convictions pursuant to Elec 302.02(h)(7); and\n\n(4) Has not had their electrician’s license or right to train as a high/medium voltage electrician suspended, revoked, or sanctioned in any jurisdiction pursuant to Elec 302.02(h)(8).\n\n(b) For the purposes of (a)(3) above, a felony conviction shall be considered disqualifying if one of the following applies:\n\n(1) The conviction involves theft, forgery, fraud, or other purpose to deprive the property of another;\n\n(2) The conviction involves perjury, unsworn falsification, or other falsification of official matters; or\n\n(3) The conviction has a direct bearing on the applicant’s ability to be licensed as an electrician.\n\n(c) An applicant who has been denied a high/medium voltage trainee identification card shall be provided an opportunity for an administrative hearing before the board in accordance with the requirements of Plc 200.\n\n(d) The initial fee for a high/medium voltage trainee identification card shall be the fee required by Plc 1002.13.\n\nSource. #10356, INTERIM, eff 6-6-13, EXPIRES: 12-3-13 (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Elec 300); ss by #10420, eff 9-25-13 (formerly Elec 302.06) (See Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Elec 300); ss by #13866, eff 4-6-24 (See Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Elec 300)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/elec100-400.html"
